cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data package, please cite it as below, together with the source studies whose samples you use."
type: software
title: "GenomicTensorSepsis: a harmonized multi-cohort blood transcriptomic resource for sepsis research"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-14
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Priyanshu
    affiliation: "Department of Biotechnology Engineering, Chandigarh University, Mohali, Punjab, India"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1576-027X"
abstract: >-
  The pipeline that finds, reprocesses, annotates, curates, validates, corrects and benchmarks the public blood
  transcriptome studies of sepsis in GEO and ArrayExpress, and packages the result: 96 studies, 12,037 sample records on
  105 study platforms, with curated labels, linked repeat deposits and patients, corrected tables and patient-safe
  benchmark splits.
license: MIT
